& [Purpose] is inspectable finite conformance evidence without authority collapse
  + admit immutable root-qualified cases and explicit coverage obligations
  + consume complete I03D ReaderPair observations without changing them
  + compare schema and typed readers only where a declared CommonSyntaxClaim makes comparison meaningful
  + repeat the complete pure evaluation and require byte-identical normalized cores

& [PrerequisiteBoundary] is strict
  + active completed I03A Revision 1 dependency proof
  + active completed I03B faithful byte ingress
  + active completed I03C residual registry
  + active completed I03D independent readers
  + exact post-I03D code snapshot dependency lock bundle registry and validator-profile identities
  + formation may proceed now but implementation cannot

& [ConformanceCase] binds one immutable expectation
  + case id root direction family fixture identity exact bytes or typed-fixture identity
  + expected ingress schema typed optional semantic and comparison dispositions
  + applicability claim ids rule ids schema locations residual ids coverage obligation ids rationale and provenance
  + changing bytes fixture claim expectation or rationale creates a successor case id

& [CommonSyntaxClaim] is the only comparison license
  + it names one shared JSON-level proposition applicable to both the selected canonical schema and selected Rust transport binding
  + it binds root kind subject rule identity expected disposition and the evidence by which each reader observes that same proposition
  + representation-only schema or typed constraints are not common claims
  + semantic residuals authority conditions and intended-use assertions are never common syntax claims unless both readers actually encode the same syntactic proposition

& [ComparisonTruthTable] is narrow
  + accepted plus accepted is agreement only when both are applicable and expected accepted for the same claim
  + rejected plus rejected is agreement only when both actually ran expected rejection and each rejection is attributable to the same declared claim
  + accepted plus rejected or rejected plus accepted is reader_disagreement
  + two rejections attributable to different rules are reason_mismatch and never agreement
  + an observation differing from its declared expectation is expectation_mismatch even if readers equal each other
  + not_applicable skipped_dependency exhausted panic and internal_fault never contribute to agreement
  + ingress refusal prevents schema and typed execution and is governed by ingress rather than treated as reader agreement

& [SemanticObservation] is outside syntax agreement
  + optional evaluation may call only an exact I03C safe_pure binding on a complete admitted fixture
  + observational_only and prohibited_authority policies never execute
  + semantic accepted refused unimplemented exhausted and internal fault remain separate
  + schema-typed agreement never implies semantic validity compatibility intended-use truth executability or authority

& [CorpusFamilies] are C00 through C07
  + C00 canonical positive and representative complete roots
  + C01 faithful byte ingress faults and limits
  + C02 object required optional null unknown type enum and tag contracts
  + C03 exact numeric token and Rust destination boundaries
  + C04 collection recursion and local-reference boundaries
  + C05 identity digest authorship and lineage substitutions
  + C06 state transition token-ring and replay mutations
  + C07 no-capability refusal external-reference and response-shape boundaries
  + each required family-root-rule relation is covered not_applicable or deferred with reviewed identity and rationale

& [CoverageObligation] is independently addressable
  + bind obligation id root rule family polarity boundary position applicability severity and source authority
  + below at and above are separate obligations
  + one case may satisfy multiple obligations only through explicit case-to-obligation edges
  + percentage is advisory; zero uncovered mandatory obligations is authoritative for a passing report

& [ResidualCoverage] preserves I03C authority
  + all twenty residual ids resolve once through the exact registry
  + each applicable residual maps to cases a reviewed not-applicable reason or an explicit deferred gap
  + I03E never upgrades unimplemented partial or observational residual disposition
  + a dangling applicable residual is a release-blocking residual_gap

& [CaseGeneration] is deterministic and reviewable
  + hand-authored seeds establish meaning
  + a bounded generator may apply one declared mutation operator to one admitted seed
  + generator identity version source case operator parameters output digest and expectation-review identity are retained
  + generated output remains a candidate until its expectation receives human review
  + random fuzz output cannot enter the canonical corpus without reduction stable identity and review

& [ExecutionDAG] is fixed
  * bind exact bundle document registry validator corpus code and lock identities
  * admit the complete corpus catalogue and coverage graph atomically
  * execute cases in lexical case-id order under checked aggregate limits
  * obtain or preserve I03B and I03D observations according to applicability
  * execute only explicitly whitelisted safe-pure semantic bindings where required
  * compare observations to expectations and common syntax claims
  * reconstruct obligation and residual coverage independently from declared summary counters
  * normalize one ReportCore
  * repeat the complete pure path from the same immutable inputs to a second ReportCore
  * compare exact normalized bytes and form one ReplayEnvelope

& [ReportCore] contains no self-reference or volatile observation
  + exact profile corpus bundle registry validator code and lock digests
  + ordered case observations comparison records semantic records findings coverage residual and resource accounts
  + disposition passed refused exhausted or internal_fault
  + no timestamp host path allocation address thread order random seed engine display text or ambient environment field

& [CanonicalEncoding] is explicit UTF-8 JSON
  + no byte-order mark no insignificant whitespace and no trailing newline
  + object member order is fixed by the report schema rather than map iteration
  + collection order is lexical by the complete normative sort key
  + integers serialize as base-10 without leading zero and no report field uses floating point
  + strings use one specified JSON escaping profile and digests use uppercase hexadecimal
  + ReportCore digest is domain-separated SHA256 over its exact canonical bytes

& [ReplayEnvelope] avoids circular digest identity
  + bind first core digest second core digest exact-byte-equality and final disposition
  + byte inequality creates nondeterminism and final internal_fault
  + the envelope digest excludes only its own digest field and is computed over a canonical envelope payload
  + a passed envelope requires identical cores and passed core disposition

& [FindingIdentity] is stable
  + finding id derives from profile case kind reader claim rule schema path residual set expected and actual stable dispositions
  + kind is expectation_mismatch reader_disagreement reason_mismatch residual_gap coverage_gap exhaustion nondeterminism or internal_fault
  + diagnostics are bounded advisory context and excluded from identity when library-generated
  + sorting is case id kind reader claim rule schema path residual ids finding id

& [Atomicity] is fail closed
  + a prerequisite identity fault prevents corpus execution
  + a case-level expected rejection is an observation and does not abort remaining cases
  + exhaustion internal fault skipped dependency or corrupt catalogue prevents a passed report
  + no partial corpus coverage or passing envelope is released

& [Limits] retain parent maxima
  + at most 4096 cases and 67108864 aggregate fixture bytes
  + at most 256 normalized findings per case
  + all ingress reader schema residual and report limits remain non-substitutive
  + every counter addition multiplication offset and allocation forecast uses checked arithmetic

& [FutureSourceTouch] must be exact at activation
  + modify cantor_procedure_tool lib.rs under the separately active schema-conformance feature
  + add conformance_report.rs
  + add one focused conformance_report integration test
  + add a content-addressed corpus catalogue and fixture tree whose every file path bytes and digest are listed in the activation lock
  + generated report bytes are test observations and are not written at runtime

& [AuthorityExclusion] is absolute
  - never: public untrusted-input API compatibility certification semantic admission Observer authority provider model service persistence runtime filesystem network notification external effect production release hardware FPGA or shared inference

& [RequestedDisposition] is preserve_then_sjs_then_form_inactive_i03e_candidate
